<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Said bin Sultan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1791">1791</a>–<a href="/years/1856">1856</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sayyid Said bin Sultan, Said ibn Sultan, Sayyid Said of Oman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Said bin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> from 1806 to 1856, the most powerful ruler of the Omani maritime empire. He extended Omani control along the East African coast, taking Mombasa from the Mazrui in 1837, and moved his court to Zanzibar, where he developed clove plantations and the caravan trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and slaves. After his death his realm was divided, creating the separate Sultanate of Zanzibar.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/said-bin-sultan.jpg" alt="Said bin Sultan" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lieutenant Henry Blosse Lynch · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Said_bin_Sultan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
